# Benefits

## Standardization

Every forecasting model consumes identical training data.

---

## Reproducibility

Training datasets can be regenerated from the same certified inputs.

---

## Fair Model Comparison

All forecasting algorithms are evaluated using equivalent datasets.

---

## Reduced Data Leakage

Time-aware dataset generation prevents future information from leaking into historical training observations.

---

## Separation of Concerns

Dataset engineering remains independent of model implementation.

---

## Future Scalability

New forecasting models can be introduced without modifying dataset preparation logic.

---

# Consequences

## Positive

- standardized supervised datasets
- simplified experimentation
- consistent model evaluation
- improved reproducibility
- reusable forecasting pipeline
- cleaner architecture
- future production readiness

---

## Trade-offs

- additional processing stage
- additional metadata management
- increased storage requirements

These trade-offs are acceptable because they improve reliability, maintainability, and scientific rigor.

---

# Alternatives Considered

## Dataset Preparation Inside Each Forecast Model

Rejected.

Reasons:

- duplicated logic
- inconsistent datasets
- unreliable benchmarking
- difficult maintenance

---

## Direct Training from Demand Intelligence

Rejected.

Reasons:

- forecasting datasets require supervised target alignment
- inconsistent horizon generation
- increased feature leakage risk
- poor experiment reproducibility

---

## Manual Dataset Construction

Rejected.

Reasons:

- error-prone
- inconsistent execution
- unsuitable for enterprise automation
- difficult governance

---

# Rationale

The Enterprise Forecast Dataset Framework establishes a clear architectural boundary between business intelligence and predictive modeling.

This separation enables:

- standardized supervised learning
- reproducible experimentation
- consistent model benchmarking
- future automated retraining
- enterprise MLOps integration
- scalable forecasting workflows

The framework also provides a foundation for future capabilities including:

- Feature Store integration
- MLflow experiment tracking
- automated model retraining
- model registry
- online inference pipelines
- real-time forecasting

---

# Decision Outcome

The AI Workforce Capacity Planning Platform formally adopts an independent Enterprise Forecast Dataset Framework.

All forecasting models must consume datasets generated by this framework.

Forecast dataset generation becomes the official enterprise mechanism for preparing training, validation, testing, and inference datasets.

This decision completes the architectural foundation required for the Enterprise Forecast Modeling Framework introduced in Implementation 11.

